WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:04.874
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Cambridge exams.

2
00:00:05.174 --> 00:00:08.781
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.081 --> 00:00:17.794
Unit fourteen: B2 First: Writing Essays, Articles and Reports. Today you will write an essay and a second task with a clear style.

4
00:00:18.094 --> 00:00:20.781
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:21.733 --> 00:00:24.838
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:25.683 --> 00:00:26.592
Essay.

7
00:00:27.583 --> 00:00:30.686
Essay means a formal piece of writing giving arguments.

8
00:00:31.283 --> 00:00:33.039
The first task is an essay.

9
00:00:33.650 --> 00:00:36.140
Your turn. Say: Essay.

10
00:00:39.000 --> 00:00:39.862
Essay.

11
00:00:40.617 --> 00:00:41.513
Article.

12
00:00:42.517 --> 00:00:45.050
Article means a piece of writing for a magazine.

13
00:00:45.650 --> 00:00:47.708
Write an article for a magazine.

14
00:00:48.317 --> 00:00:50.644
Your turn. Say: Article.

15
00:00:53.500 --> 00:00:54.199
Article.

16
00:00:54.950 --> 00:00:55.916
Review.

17
00:00:56.917 --> 00:01:00.182
Review means a text that gives an opinion about something.

18
00:01:00.783 --> 00:01:02.110
Write a film review.

19
00:01:02.717 --> 00:01:05.021
Your turn. Say: Review.

20
00:01:07.867 --> 00:01:08.786
Review.

21
00:01:09.550 --> 00:01:10.493
Report.

22
00:01:11.483 --> 00:01:14.179
Report means a formal text with sections.

23
00:01:14.783 --> 00:01:16.667
Write a report for the manager.

24
00:01:17.283 --> 00:01:20.075
Your turn. Say: Report.

25
00:01:22.933 --> 00:01:23.865
Report.

26
00:01:24.617 --> 00:01:25.420
Register.

27
00:01:26.417 --> 00:01:28.869
Register means the level of formality.

28
00:01:29.483 --> 00:01:31.332
Choose the correct register.

29
00:01:31.917 --> 00:01:34.523
Your turn. Say: Register.

30
00:01:37.367 --> 00:01:38.286
Register.

31
00:01:39.050 --> 00:01:40.515
Linking device.

32
00:01:41.517 --> 00:01:44.840
Linking device means a word or phrase that connects ideas.

33
00:01:45.450 --> 00:01:47.264
Use linking devices.

34
00:01:47.850 --> 00:01:51.141
Your turn. Say: Linking device.

35
00:01:54.000 --> 00:01:55.454
Linking device.

36
00:01:56.217 --> 00:01:57.345
Introduction.

37
00:01:58.350 --> 00:02:00.442
Introduction means the opening part.

38
00:02:01.050 --> 00:02:02.632
Write a clear introduction.

39
00:02:03.217 --> 00:02:05.753
Your turn. Say: Introduction.

40
00:02:08.600 --> 00:02:09.636
Introduction.

41
00:02:10.383 --> 00:02:11.466
Conclusion.

42
00:02:12.450 --> 00:02:14.519
Conclusion means the final part.

43
00:02:15.117 --> 00:02:16.536
End with a conclusion.

44
00:02:17.150 --> 00:02:19.512
Your turn. Say: Conclusion.

45
00:02:22.367 --> 00:02:23.484
Conclusion.

46
00:02:24.300 --> 00:02:28.601
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:29.450 --> 00:02:32.564
Visal, what are the two writing parts in B2 First?

48
00:02:33.650 --> 00:02:46.635
Part 1 is an essay that you must write: you give your opinion on a topic and explain two of three given ideas. In Part 2 you choose an email, article, report or review.

49
00:02:47.750 --> 00:02:49.332
How do I write a good essay?

50
00:02:50.417 --> 00:03:03.855
Use an introduction, two body paragraphs and a conclusion. State your opinion clearly, develop each idea with examples and use linking devices such as moreover and however.

51
00:03:04.950 --> 00:03:06.311
What about style?

52
00:03:07.417 --> 00:03:20.579
Match your register to the reader. An essay and a report are formal, an article can be lively and a letter to a friend is informal. Always write between one hundred and forty and one hundred and ninety words.

53
00:03:21.733 --> 00:03:23.408
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:24.250 --> 00:03:28.305
Grammar focus: Strategy: plan, match the register, check.

55
00:03:28.605 --> 00:03:29.919
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:30.617 --> 00:03:34.184
Moreover, public transport reduces pollution in cities.

57
00:03:35.083 --> 00:03:38.581
This report aims to describe the facilities of the sports centre.

58
00:03:39.533 --> 00:03:46.609
Plan before writing, keep to the word limit and choose a style that suits the reader. Use varied vocabulary and accurate grammar.

59
00:03:47.350 --> 00:03:50.850
Be careful! Don't say: I use slang in a report.

60
00:03:52.800 --> 00:03:55.392
Say: I use a formal register.

61
00:03:55.692 --> 00:03:57.343
Match the register.

62
00:03:58.133 --> 00:04:00.809
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

63
00:04:01.600 --> 00:04:03.007
Writing a Report.

64
00:04:03.307 --> 00:04:06.294
Sreyleak must write a report for her school director.

65
00:04:07.300 --> 00:04:11.273
She uses headings: Introduction, Facilities and Recommendation.

66
00:04:12.267 --> 00:04:15.172
She writes in a formal style without contractions.

67
00:04:16.167 --> 00:04:19.304
She uses linking words such as moreover and however.

68
00:04:20.300 --> 00:04:22.439
She checks the word count and her grammar.

69
00:04:23.533 --> 00:04:27.489
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

70
00:04:28.350 --> 00:04:30.083
The essay in Part 1 is blank.

71
00:04:30.383 --> 00:04:35.348
A, optional. B, only for Speaking. C, compulsory.

72
00:04:38.900 --> 00:04:40.923
The answer is C: compulsory.

73
00:04:42.083 --> 00:04:44.071
A report usually has blank.

74
00:04:44.371 --> 00:04:48.315
A, headings. B, emojis. C, no structure.

75
00:04:51.867 --> 00:04:53.820
The answer is A: headings.

76
00:04:54.983 --> 00:04:57.041
The register of a report is blank.

77
00:04:57.341 --> 00:05:01.122
A, slang. B, formal. C, very informal.

78
00:05:04.667 --> 00:05:06.515
The answer is B: formal.

79
00:05:07.650 --> 00:05:08.988
Moreover is a blank.

80
00:05:09.288 --> 00:05:12.976
A, noun. B, number. C, linking word.

81
00:05:16.533 --> 00:05:18.962
The answer is C: linking word.

82
00:05:20.117 --> 00:05:21.896
After writing, you should blank.

83
00:05:22.196 --> 00:05:26.453
A, check grammar and length. B, stop. C, start again.

84
00:05:30.000 --> 00:05:32.928
The answer is A: check grammar and length.

85
00:05:34.133 --> 00:05:37.378
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

86
00:05:38.217 --> 00:05:40.623
How do you plan an essay for B2 First?

87
00:05:49.417 --> 00:05:50.894
Now listen to Visal.

88
00:05:51.194 --> 00:06:05.459
I read the question and choose two of the three ideas. I plan an introduction, two body paragraphs and a conclusion, and I give examples. I use linking words and check grammar and word count.

89
00:06:05.759 --> 00:06:07.480
Excellent answer, Visal!

90
00:06:08.383 --> 00:06:13.718
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and strategy: plan, match the register, check.

91
00:06:14.018 --> 00:06:18.284
Today's value is preparedness. Get ready before an emergency happens.

92
00:06:18.584 --> 00:06:21.004
See you in Unit fifteen. Goodbye!

93
00:06:21.304 --> 00:06:23.608
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

